-## r6 → r7 rework (Perkins review 4977695071 — 2 blockers, both resolved)
-
-- **1 (temp-path race carried since r3 — NOT closed):** macOS returns IDENTICAL nanosecond values for back-to-back calls, so the ns-only suffix still collided under the parallel runner (Perkins: 1 failure in 30 pristine runs; a shared path + one test's `os.remove` deleting another's fixture). The suffix is now **ns + 4 crypto-random bytes** and the path is **NEVER pre-removed** — it is fresh by construction, so no parallel test can ever own it. 6/6 + the gate-2 ×3 repeat leg green.
-- **2 (effect_settings_adjust — the r5 trap, ADJUST TWIN):** the pure helpers were pinned but the WIRING shipped unpinned (deleting the palette apply / ui_scale apply / settings_save was 18/18 green at r6). Four exec-level legs drive `effect_settings_adjust` itself (the chip-click test pattern): palette (state + effective-palette remap + **the persisted file asserted via a path-injected `settings_save_at`**), motion (view flag + persisted), scale (view factor + persisted), audio (mute). **Revert-style control verified:** deleting the applies + save fails 3 tests.
+- **Core events, not app-side calls.** Rule 1 says "extend the map" — the map is keyed on `pp.Event` tags, so wire/spawn became real append-only zero-payload tags. This keeps the audio golden's vacuous-guard doctrine (W3/W4: the golden must PROVE each kind fired) and the replay gate meaningful; app-side-only calls would have been unpinnable by the harness.
+- **Wire click ≠ router placement.** The four interactions in the briefing are pipe drawn, growth spawn, crisis, delivery. Player router placement is a deliberate action with its own placement ghost/pop visual — it stays silent (could reuse the wire click later if the fun-test wants it).
+- **No captions for the new cues.** Rule 4 (no visual/palette changes) — captions are view-layer. Wire/spawn have strong visual feedback already (the pipe appears; the spawn-feel telegraph+reveal). The a11y contract's "caption every ALERT" is unchanged.
+- **`audio_spawn.dem` exists because `audio.dem`'s delicate surge recipe must not gain growth.** Growth would shift the era-3 bottleneck saturation and move the crisis timing; a third T1-only audio-family demo pins the spawn path instead.
+- **Parity's `sim_events` stays nil deliberately** — parity dispatches all frames before its step loop, so a dispatch-time event would land before the hash mark and never ride the pinned stream; the audio goldens pin the wire/spawn events through step's own emissions. Commented in `harness/parity.odin`.
+- **Asset contract extended:** `assets/audio/wire_01..03.ogg` + `spawn_01..03.ogg` drop-in slots (README updated; placeholders synthesized in `synth_wav`).
